  "title": "Avoid Jumping to Conclusions About Interest",
  "description": "Avoid jumping to conclusions about interest. Here’s how: - Observe behavior: Look for clear, consistent signals before making assumptions. - Ask directly: If appropriate, communicate openly rather than guessing intentions. - Avoid projecting: Separate your feelings from how you think others perceive you. Example: Instead of assuming someone is interested based on a smile, look for repeated and direct signs of interest.",
